    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `checkDigit` as a derived response field \u2014 the Luhn check digit over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`.\n\nI followed the existing pattern for computed, non-stored fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `identityKey`), which are derived at DTO-mapping time from delegated util classes rather than persisted on the entity:\n\n1. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility utility with `checkDigit(String)` that runs the Luhn algorithm over the digits of any string (ignoring non-digit separators like the `-` in `LON-SMI-0007`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a small `checkDigit(Owner)` delegate that calls `Luhn.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, matching how the other derived fields are wired.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property (int, 0\u20139, `readOnly`) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and it appears in the response.\n\nNo new entity column or storage was needed since `checkDigit` is fully derivable from the already-stored `customerCode`, keeping the logic where it belongs and avoiding duplicating the Luhn routine.",
